# Accepted findings, each a deliberate trade-off documented in the README.

# The ALB is the public entry point of an internet-facing API.
AVD-AWS-0053

# Plain HTTP is only served when no ACM certificate is configured (demo mode);
# with certificate_arn set, HTTP redirects to HTTPS (TLS 1.3 policy).
AVD-AWS-0054

# HTTPS egress to anywhere is required: merchant callback URLs are arbitrary hosts.
aws-vpc-no-public-egress-sgr

# No NAT gateway (cost): app instances get public IPs but accept traffic only
# from the ALB security group and have no SSH (SSM Session Manager instead).
aws-vpc-no-public-ingress-sgr

# AWS-managed keys instead of customer-managed KMS keys ($1/key/month each);
# ALB access-log delivery only supports SSE-S3 anyway.
AVD-AWS-0132
AVD-AWS-0136
